Chapter: MountainsCheck
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Safari chapter Camera
  cites Safari chapter Paint
  cites Safari chapter Sky
  cites Safari chapter Mountains
  cites Judge chapter Grade
  cites Gold chapter MountainsGold

 Grade the Mountains port against wasm/mountains.zig.

 Two seams. The crest and the headlight test are seam 1, walked over a table of
 bearings; draw is seam 3, decoded off paint's wire.

 THE COLOURS ARE GRADED EXACTLY, as in Sky and for the same reason: dimmed and
 snowColor round a channel and pack three of them, which is precisely the work the
 zig plug could not emit before row 2.03. A dimmed rock one off is a wrong rock.

 THE SILHOUETTE COORDINATES ARE WHERE THE RANGE FUNCTIONS ARE REALLY GRADED.
 northRange, westRange and groundBase are private to the module, so nothing can
 call them directly -- but every silhouette traces one of them over 681 columns,
 so 683-point polygons carry them. This is also the only place in the port that
 grades an ARC TANGENT: bearing-at calls r-atan once per column, so a wrong atan
 would bend every ridge.

 THE CASES ARE BRANCHES. A plain forward view; a heading swung onto the west
 range, which puts the north range off-screen so that NO column clears its
 snowline and drawSnow takes its `m < 2` bail -- that case emits three polygons
 where the others emit four, and the count is the assertion; a pulled-in focal,
 which changes the angular span and v_scale together and shrinks the snow band
 from 88 points to 62; and full night, where the rock is at its dimmest.

 683 is 681 columns plus the two points that close the polygon down to the
 horizon. Both sides walk exactly 681 because the column loop steps by 2.0 from
 -200.0, and both are exact in binary. The one loop that is NOT exact is the
 snow peak's 0.01 -- see the note in the port; it moves the peak by 5.8e-8
 relative and cannot move a point count.

 We say:

Section: Scalars

  bearings : List Real
  bearings = [0.0, 0.2, 0.0 - 0.2, 0.5, 0.94, 0.0 - 0.94, 0.96, 0.0 - 0.96, 0.0 - 2.0416, 0.0 - 1.7, 0.0 - 2.4, 0.0 - 2.76, 0.0 - 1.32, 0.0 - 2.2176, 3.0, 0.0 - 3.0, 3.14, 0.0 - 3.14, 1.5, 0.0 - 1.5]

  dusks : List Real
  dusks = [0.0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 0.9, 1.0]

 The probe reads the colour of the FIRST polygon of each frame, which is the
 westward range, so this is dimmed rock-west at each dusk.

  rocks : List Real, Integer -> List Integer
  rocks (ds) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ds then []
    else [dimmed rock-west (list-at ds i)] & rocks ds (i + 1)

  steps : List Real
  steps = [0.0, 2000.0, 3500.0, 3900.0, 4000.0, 4300.0, 5000.0, 8000.0]

Section: The Frames

  frame-1 : List DrawCmd
  frame-1 = draw 0.0 0.0 focal camera-w

  frame-2 : List DrawCmd
  frame-2 = draw (0.0 - 2.0416) 0.35 focal camera-w

  frame-3 : List DrawCmd
  frame-3 = draw 0.6 0.6 (focal * 0.45) camera-w

  frame-4 : List DrawCmd
  frame-4 = draw 0.0 1.0 focal camera-w

  all-cmds : List DrawCmd
  all-cmds = frame-1 & frame-2 & frame-3 & frame-4

  cmd-tags : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Integer
  cmd-tags (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else [(list-at cs i).tag] & cmd-tags cs (i + 1)

  cmd-colors : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Integer
  cmd-colors (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else [(list-at cs i).color] & cmd-colors cs (i + 1)

  cmd-counts : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Integer
  cmd-counts (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else [list-length (list-at cs i).pts / 2] & cmd-counts cs (i + 1)

 EVERY 8th POINT, matching the probe. Four frames at full density are 16,868
 coordinates, and codexzig exhausts its own 4 GiB bump heap on a Real literal that
 size -- the heap never reclaims, so the gold a single unit can carry has a
 ceiling. Striding is what to give up: the point COUNTS above are still exact, so
 a silhouette that gained or lost a column still fails hard, and 86 samples across
 a curve that is smooth by construction still catch a wrong range function, a
 wrong arc tangent, a wrong bearing mapping or a wrong v-scale.

  stride-pts : List Real, Integer -> List Real
  stride-pts (ps) (i) =
    if i * 2 >= list-length ps then []
    else [list-at ps (i * 2), list-at ps (i * 2 + 1)] & stride-pts ps (i + 8)

  cmd-coords : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Real
  cmd-coords (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else (stride-pts (list-at cs i).pts 0) & cmd-coords cs (i + 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "mt-crest      " (list-map horizon-crest-px bearings) g-mt-crest 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "mt-rock       " (rocks dusks 0) g-mt-rock)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "mt-sun-behind " (list-map sun-behind-mountains steps) g-mt-sun-behind)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "mt-tags       " (cmd-tags all-cmds 0) g-mt-tags)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "mt-colors     " (cmd-colors all-cmds 0) g-mt-colors)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "mt-counts     " (cmd-counts all-cmds 0) g-mt-counts)
    print-line-uni (grade-px    "mt-coords     " (cmd-coords all-cmds 0) g-mt-coords 0.001 0.000001)
  end
